# Snyk policy for platform/ (scanned via `snyk test --file=poetry.lock`).
#
# The four permanent ignores below (no `expires`) share one basis: the researcher reports
# Snyk cites (gists published 2026-03-21) and the matching GitHub advisories state the
# flaw affects litellm <= 1.82.2 ("latest at time of discovery"). Snyk records the range
# as [0,] with no fix, so it flags the locked 1.103.x anyway. Also, the flaws are in the
# litellm proxy server (litellm/proxy/...), which this repo never runs (client library
# only: llm-provider-config / controls-compliance-catalog). Decided 2026-10-31.
version: v1.25.0
ignore:
  SNYK-PYTHON-LITELLM-17391451:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          Permanent. Researcher report and GitHub advisory (GHSA-mf52-j94g-746m) give
          the affected range as litellm <= 1.82.2; Snyk's [0,] range is overbroad.
          Flaw is in the proxy server (proxy/auth/login_utils.py), never run here.
        created: 2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z
  SNYK-PYTHON-LITELLM-17391455:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          Permanent. Researcher report and GitHub advisory (GHSA-qmf3-4767-5fg3) give
          the affected range as litellm <= 1.82.2; Snyk's [0,] range is overbroad.
          Flaw is in the proxy server (M2M JWT handler), never run here.
        created: 2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z
  SNYK-PYTHON-LITELLM-17393717:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          Permanent. Researcher report and GitHub advisory (GHSA-j37q-q7p9-vpwm) give
          the affected range as litellm <= 1.82.2; Snyk's [0,] range is overbroad.
          Flaw is in the proxy server (SSO debug endpoints), never run here.
        created: 2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z
  SNYK-PYTHON-LITELLM-17393719:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          Permanent. Researcher report and GitHub advisory (GHSA-w2mh-qq9q-453x) give
          the affected range as litellm <= 1.82.2; Snyk's [0,] range is overbroad.
          Flaw is in the proxy server (SSO login session tokens), never run here.
        created: 2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z
  SNYK-PYTHON-LITELLM-20257373:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          litellm is used only as a client library (completion calls via
          llm-provider-config / controls-compliance-catalog); the litellm proxy
          server these advisories concern is never run. No fixed release exists
          (1.105.0, the locked version, is still affected as of 2026-10-12).
          Re-review on expiry.
        expires: 2026-11-30T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z
  SNYK-PYTHON-LITELLM-20840174:
    - '*':
        reason: >-
          CVE-2026-108575 (Red Hat Bugzilla 2549217): improper authorization via
          the api_key argument to litellm's get_secret (os.environ/NAME references),
          reported up to 1.94.0, no vendor fix known. This is SDK code, not proxy-only.
          Mitigated in first-party code: llm-provider-config refuses os.environ/...
          values as API keys on store and on use (credentials.py), so no user input
          can reach get_secret as an api_key reference. Re-review on expiry.
        expires: 2026-11-30T00:00:00.000Z
        created: 2026-10-31T00:00:00.000Z
